   "id": 669151,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"8\">\n  <li>Technology required. Use the three graphs to answer questions a–c. Then, use graphing technology to check each equation.</li>\n</ol>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n        <tbody><tr>\n            <td>\n                <p>Graph A</p>\n                <img alt=\"Parabola. Opens up. X intercepts = 0 and -7.\" height=\"211\" src=\"exercises/media/67fc174afbc0b597.svg\" width=\"267\">\n            </td>\n            <td>\n                <p>Graph B</p>\n                <img alt=\"Parabola. Opens up. Vertex = 0 comma -16. X intercepts = -4 and 4.\" height=\"215\" src=\"exercises/media/d705fec31f03b523.svg\" width=\"264\">\n            </td>\n            <td>\n                <p>Graph C</p>\n                <img alt=\"Parabola. Opens up. X intercepts = -9 and 3.\" height=\"216\" src=\"exercises/media/f02daec9333de869.svg\" width=\"270\">\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody></table>\n<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" type=\"a\">\n  <li>Which graph represents the equation <span data-math=\"f(x)=x(x+7)\">f(x)=x(x+7)</span> or <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2+7x\">f(x)=x^2+7x</span>? Then, use graphing technology to check your answer.</li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1333998,
     "content_html": "Graph A"
    },
    {
     "id": 1333999,
     "content_html": "Graph B"
    },
    {
     "id": 1334000,
     "content_html": "Graph C"
    }
   ],
